Per-filament lists read past their end. Projects can carry fewer values than filaments: Bambu's CLI keeps
single values for keys no loaded preset sets (filament_change_length_nc, ...) and sets 45 mm³ on every value
of the filament_prime_volume list it has. Print::_make_wipe_tower (filament_prime_volume(_nc)) and WipeTower
(filament_change_length(_nc)) index those lists directly, reading past the vector: in practice the zeroed
bytes after a small allocation, in general whatever the heap holds (found with AddressSanitizer). Read 0 past
the end explicitly; Bambu Studio's own output for those projects is unchanged (tests/expected.json).

